# Watcher API Configuration
# This API key authenticates Claude Code hooks when sending events to the /events endpoint
#
# Format: watcher_sk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# The "watcher_sk_" prefix helps identify the key type and purpose
#
# To use:
# 1. Copy this file to .env
# 2. Generate a secure random key (minimum 32 characters recommended)
# 3. Replace the value below with your generated key
# 4. Ensure .env is in .gitignore to prevent committing secrets
#
# Example generation (run in terminal):
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#   # Then prepend "watcher_sk_" to the output
WATCHER_API_KEY=watcher_sk_CHANGE_ME

# Server Configuration
# Port the observability server listens on
# Default: 3008
# SERVER_PORT=3008

# Database Configuration
# Path to SQLite database file (relative to server working directory)
# Default: ./data/events.db
# DB_PATH=./data/events.db

# Logging
# Log level: debug, info, warn, error
# Default: info
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# Hook Configuration for Remote Watcher Server
# =============================================
#
# To configure Claude Code hooks to send events to this remote Watcher server:
#
# 1. Export the WATCHER_API_KEY environment variable (generated from this .env file):
#    export WATCHER_API_KEY=<your-key-from-above>
#
# 2. Update your project's .claude/settings.json to point hooks to the remote server:
#    Example for watcher.flipgoal.xyz deployment:
#
#    {
#      "hooks": {
#        "notification": {
#          "enabled": true,
#          "handler": "~/.claude/hooks/notification.py",
#          "args": "--server-url https://watcher.flipgoal.xyz/events --event-type Notification"
#        },
#        "stop": {
#          "enabled": true,
#          "handler": "~/.claude/hooks/stop.py",
#          "args": "--server-url https://watcher.flipgoal.xyz/events --event-type Stop"
#        },
#        "subagent_stop": {
#          "enabled": true,
#          "handler": "~/.claude/hooks/subagent_stop.py",
#          "args": "--server-url https://watcher.flipgoal.xyz/events --event-type SubagentStop"
#        }
#      }
#    }
#
# 3. The --server-url flag accepts:
#    - Local server: http://localhost:3008/events (default)
#    - Remote server: https://your-domain.com/events
#
# 4. Ensure WATCHER_API_KEY is set in your environment before running Claude Code.
#    The hooks automatically include it in the Authorization header:
#    Authorization: Bearer <WATCHER_API_KEY>
#
# Security Notes:
# - Never commit .env files to version control
# - Rotate API keys periodically
# - Use environment variables to pass keys, not command-line arguments
# - The server validates the API key on every request to /events endpoint
